# The git hooks are POSIX sh scripts: LF line endings in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says.
scripts/git-hooks/* text eol=lf
# What a release ships, LF in every checkout too (M7-REL-1): with core.autocrlf on, a checkout would otherwise write the
# extension and the CSS with CRLF while git status calls the tree clean. Releases read HEAD's bytes either way; this
# keeps the working tree, which local-test and the dev build package, the same bytes. Binary files stay as they are.
extension/** text=auto eol=lf
css/** text=auto eol=lf
